-- title:
--   Two minimal primes in the geometric pole chart at level Np
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N$ and $p$ with $N \neq 0$ and $p$ prime, and assume $p \nmid N$. Write $\mathbf{Z}_{(p)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbf{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ equipped with a $\mathbf{Z}_{(p)}$-algebra structure. Let $F$ denote the field `modularFunctionFieldFull (N * p)`, let $j \in F$ be the element `jFull (N * p)` given by the modular function `jq`, and let $\mathcal{O} =$ `chartAlgInf (N * p) p` be the $\mathbf{Z}_{(p)}$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of all elements of $F$ that are integral over the $\mathbf{Z}_{(p)}$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$, i.e. the integral closure of $\mathbf{Z}_{(p)}[1/j]$ in $F$. The assertion is that the set of minimal prime ideals of the ring $\kappa \otimes_{\mathbf{Z}_{(p)}} \mathcal{O}$ is finite and that its cardinality (as a `Set.ncard`) equals $2$.
--
--   This is the statement that the geometric special fibre of the pole chart ($1/j$ chart) of the Igusa-type integral model at level $Np$, $p \nmid N$, has exactly two irreducible components, in the form of a count of minimal primes after base change to an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$; over $\mathbf{F}_p$ the corresponding count, together with reducedness, is supplied by `isReduced_quotient_and_ncard_minimalPrimes_span_natCast_of_not_dvd`, while the embeddings of the components into Laurent series furnished by `exists_ringHom_laurentSeries_ker_eq_of_mem_minimalPrimes_of_not_dvd` control the behaviour under the base change to $\kappa$. It is used in the full-level analysis of the $1/j$ chart, in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.jInvChartInf_not_mem_of_exists_two_minimalPrimes_span_le_chartAlgInf_laurentBaseChange_gamma0_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.jInvChartInf_not_mem_of_exists_two_minimalPrimes_span_le_chartAlgInf_laurentBaseChange_gamma0_mul).
